<header class="sp-head"><p class="featured-region">1873 · Monroe County, New York</p><h1 class="sp-title">Susan B. Anthony on Women's Right to Vote</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/susan-b-anthony">Susan B. Anthony</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>Susan B. Anthony was arrested for voting in the presidential election of 1872. Before her trial she toured the county, arguing that the Constitution already guaranteed women the vote.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The words</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>It was we, the people; not we, the white male citizens; nor yet we, the male citizens; but we, the whole people, who formed the Union.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">Speech given across Monroe County, New York, 1873.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>Anthony was convicted and fined 100 dollars, which she refused to pay. She died in 1906; the Nineteenth Amendment, which gave American women the vote in 1920, was popularly known as the Anthony Amendment.</p></section>
